. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3
. 
.         /* Description of the model for H3
>                 
>         Our dependent variable for testing H3 (effect of having daughters on 
> gender equality as measured by behavior/outcomes) is the within-household sha
> re of women-specific stereotypical activities that are conducted by men. We c
> onsider 4 groups of activities: childcare, care for other persons, housework 
> and running errands. We compute the number of hours declared by each member o
> f the household in such activities throughout the week from the corresponding
>  survey items, and then compute how much of the within-household total hours 
> men declare spending time in such activities.
>         
>         We hypothesize that, conditional on having kids, having a daughter is
>  a random event. Thus, we do not add control variables in the regression. 
>         
>         We consider a tobit model with both upper (at 1) and lower (at 0) cen
> shorships with our measure of gender equality within the household as depende
> nt variable and a binary variable for having at least one daughter as indepen
> dent variable.
>         
>         Further, we run the model only on observations that are not tagged fo
> r H3.      
>         
>         In order to correct for multiple hypothesis testing (FWER), we also r
> un the 3 other regressions (see the other .do files for a description of the 
> models).
>         
>         
>         */
.         
.         rwolf2 /// Multiple-Hypothesis Testing correction
>         (tobit dep_var_h1 d_daughter if h1_tag == 0, ll(0) ul(1)) /// Model f
> or H1
>         (tobit dep_var_h2 d_daughter if h2_tag == 0, ll(0) ul(1)) /// Model f
> or H2
>         (tobit dep_var_h3 d_daughter if h3_tag == 0, ll(0) ul(1)) /// Model f
> or H3
>         (tobit dep_var_h4 i.sex i.d_daughter int_sex_daughter if h4_tag == 0,
>  ll(0) ul(1)) /// Model for H4
>         , indepvars(d_daughter, d_daughter, d_daughter, int_sex_daughter) one
> sided(positive) reps(1000)
